    "q-96730": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96730",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that $X∼B(9,0.3),$ compute $P(X\\le 7).$ Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(9,0.3),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{9}{x})(0.3)^{x}(0.7)^{9-x}.\n$$\n\nComputing $P(X\\le 7)$ will require us to compute $f(x)$ at $x=0,1,2,…,7.$ However, if we compute the complement $P(X>7)$ instead, then we will only have to compute $f(x)$ at $x=8,9,$ which will result in a much faster computation.\n\nComputing $P(X>7),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>7) & =P(X\\in \\{8,9\\}) \\\\  & =f(8)+f(9) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{9}{8})(0.3)^{8}(0.7)^{9-8}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{9}{9})(0.3)^{9}(0.7)^{9-9} \\\\  & =9(0.3)^{8}(0.7)+(0.3)^{9} \\\\  & ≈0.0004\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 7) & =1-P(X>7) \\\\  & ≈1-0.0004 \\\\  & =0.9996\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
